<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Rafai</h1><p class="st-meta">1870 CE – 1909 CE (approx.) · capital Rafai</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Zande sultanate on the Mbomou River whose rulers traded ivory and captives before falling under French rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Rafai state was one of several Zande-ruled sultanates that formed along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbomou-river">Mbomou River</a> in the 19th century. It took its name from its ruler Rafai, whose followers controlled the area around the town that still bears the name.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is recorded in detail. Like its neighbours, the sultanate depended on armed retainers, tribute and the sale of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and captives to traders coming from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> basin, which supplied firearms.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 1890s it dealt with officers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a> and then, after the 1894 boundary agreement, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Its independent power ended when it was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ubangi-shari">Ubangi-Shari</a> in the early 20th century.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="sultanate, 1870 CE – 1909 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">sultanate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.92%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1870 CE – 1909 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Rafai</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rafai</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pazande</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/central-african-republic">Central African Republic</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rafai</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=sultanate-of-rafai" aria-label="Sultanate of Rafai on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5255 1920 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sultanate of Rafai lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5515 2270h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5575 2176h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5575 2176h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Central African Republic. <a href="/atlas?year=1890&amp;focus=sultanate-of-rafai">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

